# Bria, Riptide Rogue: prowess and her "whenever you cast a noncreature spell" trigger both care about noncreature spells only.
# With Bria in play Bot1 casts a Memnite (a creature spell): nothing triggers. Then a Mox Jet (noncreature): Bria's own prowess,
# the prowess she gives the Memnite and her unblockable trigger go on the stack, the trigger targeting Bria herself (a creature
# Bot1 controls). Both creatures are pumped until end of turn only: on turn 3 Bria is a 3/3 again, the Memnite a 1/1, and the
# "can't be blocked this turn" has ended, so Bot2's Ornithopter blocks Bria.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Bria, Riptide Rogue
Memnite
Mox Jet
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x19

